# ================================================================
# BOB's side of the conversation.
#
# Run order:
#   1. "1. Create bob" below  -> stores {{bobId}} globally
#      (needs {{jimId}} + {{chatUuid}} from jim.http steps 1-2 first)
#   2. run the rest top-to-bottom, then back to jim.http step 4.
#
# Rooms are identified by uuid now — pair order no longer matters.
# ================================================================

### 1. Create bob
POST http://{{host}}:{{port}}/users
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "bob"
}

> {%
    client.global.set("bobId", response.body.id);
%}

### 2. Reply to jim
POST http://{{host}}:{{port}}/chat/{{chatUuid}}/messages
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "senderId": {{bobId}},
  "text": "hey jim, bob here!"
}

### 3. Read the room (should show both messages)
GET http://{{host}}:{{port}}/chat/{{chatUuid}}/messages

# --- live socket (needs an IDE version with WebSocket .http support) ---
# Open this alongside jim.http's socket, then send here and watch
# jim's socket receive it.
# WEBSOCKET ws://{{host}}:{{port}}/chat/{{chatUuid}}
#
# === send text
# {"senderId": {{bobId}}, "text": "live from bob"}
